# Command Beacon's second ability (CR 903.3, 903.9b): with two designated commanders in Bot1's command zone, Bot1
# chooses one to put into hand; the other stays in the command zone, as does Bot2's commander. (The scenario harness does
# not validate deck construction, so the pair need not be printed partners; the two-commander choice is the point.) The
# land taps for {C} first and later pays {T} and sacrifices itself, so the pool is empty after each payment.

[Format]
Commander
[Bot1 Commander]
Rograkh, Son of Rohgahh
Kytheon, Hero of Akros
[Bot2 Commander]
Raging Goblin
[Bot1 Deck]
Command Beacon
Mountain x39
[Bot2 Deck]
Island x40
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Command Beacon.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Command Beacon.Activate(Ability: {C})
? Bot1.Mana = {C}
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Command Beacon.Activate(Ability: Put your commander)
! Bot1.Choose(Raging Goblin)
Bot1.Choose(Kytheon, Hero of Akros)
? Bot1.Mana =

[Expect]
Bot1.Command = Rograkh, Son of Rohgahh
Bot1.Command.Count = 1
Bot2.Command = Raging Goblin
Bot1.Hand.Count = 8
Bot1.Battlefield.Command Beacon = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Command Beacon
